<%- include('../partials/header') %>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="separator">/</span>
      <span>FAQ</span>
    </div>

    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-10);">Everything you need to know about the DIY Credit Report Guide and the credit education process.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <!-- Guide & Product FAQs -->
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What exactly is included in the guide?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            The DIY Credit Report &amp; Credit Building Guide is a 50+ page PDF that covers: understanding credit reports and scores, reviewing your reports for errors, the dispute process for all three credit bureaus, fraud alerts and credit freezes, identity theft recovery, credit building strategies, and your consumer rights. It also includes dispute letter templates, checklists, and a glossary of terms.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How is this guide different from hiring a credit repair company?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Credit repair companies charge monthly fees (often $50–$150/month) to dispute items on your behalf. They act as a middleman between you and the credit bureaus. This guide teaches you how to do it yourself with a one-time payment of $29. You maintain full control of the process and save money. We do not perform any actions on your behalf.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Will this guide fix my credit?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            This is an educational guide — not a service that fixes credit. We provide information, instructions, and templates, but we cannot and do not promise any specific outcomes. Many consumers have successfully disputed errors on their own using similar methods, but results depend on the accuracy of your reports and your own efforts. We make no guarantees about credit score improvements.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Purchasing FAQs -->
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How do I purchase the guide?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Visit the <a href="/product">Product page</a> and click the "Buy Now" button. You'll be taken to a secure Stripe checkout page where you can pay with a credit or debit card. After successful payment, you'll be redirected to a download page.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What payment methods do you accept?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            We process payments through Stripe, which accepts Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover, and other major credit and debit cards. Apple Pay and Google Pay may also be available depending on your browser.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How do I receive the guide after purchasing?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Immediately after purchase, you'll be taken to a success page with a download button. We'll also send a download link to the email address you provided during checkout. The download link expires after 7 days for security purposes, so please download and save the PDF promptly.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Is my payment information secure?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Yes. All payments are processed through Stripe, a PCI-compliant payment processor. We never see or store your full credit card details on our servers. Your payment information is handled entirely by Stripe's secure infrastructure.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Refund FAQs -->
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What is your refund policy?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            We offer a 7-day refund policy. If you believe the guide does not match its description, contact us within 7 days of purchase and we'll review your request. Refunds are processed on a case-by-case basis. See our <a href="/refund">full Refund Policy</a> for details.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How do I request a refund?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            To request a refund, please <a href="/support">contact our support team</a> and provide your order details (email used at purchase and approximate purchase date). We'll review your request and respond within 2-3 business days.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Credit Education FAQs -->
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Do I need any special knowledge to use this guide?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            No. The guide is written in plain English and designed for beginners. If you can read and follow step-by-step instructions, you can use this guide effectively. No legal or financial background is required.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How long does the dispute process usually take?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            By law, credit bureaus have 30 days (with a possible 15-day extension) to investigate disputes. Results typically arrive within 30-45 days after submitting a dispute. However, this varies depending on the complexity of your dispute and the bureau's workload.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Can I dispute items on someone else's behalf?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Generally, you can only dispute items on your own credit reports. If you need to help a family member (like an elderly parent), you may need power of attorney or written authorization. The guide explains the process for individuals managing their own credit.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What is the difference between a credit freeze and a fraud alert?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            A credit freeze restricts access to your credit report, making it difficult for identity thieves to open new accounts in your name. It's free and remains in place until you lift it. A fraud alert is a notice on your credit report asking lenders to verify your identity before opening accounts. It's also free and lasts for one year (or 7 years with an identity theft report). Both are explained in detail in the guide.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Support -->
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>I still have questions. How can I get help?</span>
          <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            You can visit our <a href="/support">Support page</a> to use the AI chat assistant (for general questions) or submit a contact form. Our support team typically responds within 1-2 business days.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>